    {
      "id": 16149,
      "name": "robb8888",
      "username": "robb8888",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-02-06T04:15:01.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I just unlocked Hunted Naturalist, and had a question about his base power. &nbsp;The card reads in pertinent part:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\"Select [Croc], [Gazelle], or [Rhino]. &nbsp;Until the end of your next turn, you may activate that icon's effects.\" &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So if The Naturalist is in (ex:) Croc form, and uses his power to \"activate\" (ex:) Gazelle Form, that means until the end of his next turn, he can activate *both* Croc and Gazelle's effects, or either/or? &nbsp; For example, if I played Primal Charge, would he both draw 4 cards (Gazelle) and deal a target 3 DMG (Croc), or would he have to choose from one of those effects? &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As I read the text of Hunted Naturalist's base power, I tend to think he can do both: &nbsp;The text of his base power does not say \"...you may ONLY activate that icon's effects...\", and none of the cards with animal-form effects have any language saying \"only one of the effects below,\" or anything similar. &nbsp;And this would seem to be in keeping with the \"story\" behind the variant, which is that Naturalist is losing control of his transformations, and is close to becoming some sort of strange hybrid Croco-Gazelle-Rhino.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Are there any official rulings to the contrary? &nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:46.307Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
