      "raw": "<p>I just unlocked Hunted Naturalist, and had a question about his base power. &nbsp;The card reads in pertinent part:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&quot;Select [Croc], [Gazelle], or [Rhino]. &nbsp;Until the end of your next turn, you may activate that icon&#39;s effects.&quot; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So if The Naturalist is in (ex:) Croc form, and uses his power to &quot;activate&quot; (ex:) Gazelle Form, that means until the end of his next turn, he can activate *both* Croc and Gazelle&#39;s effects, or either/or? &nbsp; For example, if I played Primal Charge, would he both draw 4 cards (Gazelle) and deal a target 3 DMG (Croc), or would he have to choose from one of those effects? &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As I read the text of Hunted Naturalist&#39;s base power, I tend to think he can do both: &nbsp;The text of his base power does not say &quot;...you may ONLY activate that icon&#39;s effects...&quot;, and none of the cards with animal-form effects have any language saying &quot;only one of the effects below,&quot; or anything similar. &nbsp;And this would seem to be in keeping with the &quot;story&quot; behind the variant, which is that Naturalist is losing control of his transformations, and is close to becoming some sort of strange hybrid Croco-Gazelle-Rhino.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Are there any official rulings to the contrary? &nbsp;</p>",
