    {
      "id": 188734,
      "name": "robb8888",
      "username": "robb8888",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-02-07T17:57:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Platypus or Turducken, how ever you want to spell it, it's outstanding. &nbsp; I played him in a couple of matches yesterday, and I think I prefer him to Base Naturalist. &nbsp;In base Naturalist, it seems that sometimes you get \"stuck\" in a Form -- tanking in Rhino, for example -- and want to occasionally want to get in a Crocodile attack, or use Gazelle to draw cards/get rid of Ongoings/deck control, but don't want to lose Rhino's benefits. &nbsp;Hunted Naturalist totally solves that problem. &nbsp;It takes a few card draws to get him going, but between Shifter's Strength, Primal Charge (Gazelle) and Natural Form Power (Gazelle), he has massive card draw, and can hunt up (no pun intended) the cards he needs in no time. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The results when I first \"platypused\" him were mind-boggling. &nbsp;How many other heroes can in *one* turn (here via Bestial Shift/Natural Form's Power/Natural Born Vigor): &nbsp;(a) heal themselves 5 HP; (b) draw two extra cards (or let another hero do so); (c) get an extra card play; (d) play three powers; (c) give themselves -1 DR; and (d) deal 3 toxic damage, 3 melee damage, and (x2) 1 toxic damage? &nbsp; If you combine him with AA, PW Fanatic or Parse for even more extra power uses, it's ridiculous. &nbsp; I played a game against Dawn in Insula Primalis and just tore her down, particularly when the Obsidian Fields started popping up. &nbsp;THN may be my new favorite hero. &nbsp; If he only had some enviroment destruction, he'd be perfect (...but of course, he then wouldn't be \"The Naturalist,\" would he?)</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:14:45.764Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
