      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-02-07T20:08:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I've had Turducken once when a local restaurant was serving a fancy version for Thanksgiving. &nbsp;It's surprisingly good.</p><p>It's a deboned turkey wrapped around a deboned duck wrapped around a deboned chicken, with layers of stuffing inbetween the fowls. &nbsp;The whole assembly is then tied and roasted, then cut like a loaf so each slice gets part of each type of meat.</p><p><a href=\"https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/548-turducken\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"><span>https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/548-turducken</span></a></p><p><span>[I suspect the Naturalist would disapprove - or then again, maybe not]</span></p>",
