      "raw": "<p>I&#39;ve had Turducken once when a local restaurant was serving a fancy version for Thanksgiving. &nbsp;It&#39;s surprisingly good.</p><p>It&#39;s a deboned turkey wrapped around a deboned duck wrapped around a deboned chicken, with layers of stuffing inbetween the fowls. &nbsp;The whole assembly is then tied and roasted, then cut like a loaf so each slice gets part of each type of meat.</p><p><a href=\"https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/548-turducken\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/548-turducken</span></a></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">[I suspect the Naturalist would disapprove - or then again, maybe not]</span></p>",
